## Fix Apps graph writes for SWRL apply and inference purge

Context: On Databricks Apps the warehouse client is INLINE Statement
Execution, which only implemented `execute_query`. Explorer Apply SWRL and
Purge both call `execute_statement` (CREATE/INSERT/TRUNCATE plus graph-index
rebuild). That raised `AttributeError`, shown as "Writing inferred triples
to the graph failed" or the generic "An internal error occurred".

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/StatementExecutionWarehouse.py
   Add `execute_statement` (same SEA path as reads) and
   `uses_inline_statements`.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   Route all DDL/DML through `run_sql` (statement, else query).
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   INSERT via SEA instead of Thrift when Apps INLINE is in use; purge
   returns 0 if the inferred companion table does not exist yet.
4. tests/units/core/test_statement_execution_warehouse.py
   Contract that DDL reuses `execute_query`.
5. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py
   `run_sql` falls back to `execute_query`.
6. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_flat_store.py
   Apps inserts do not open a Thrift session.
7. tests/units/graphdb/test_materialized_inference_purge.py
   Missing inferred companion purges as a no-op.
8. docs/data-access.md
   Document Apps companion writes over Statement Execution.

